# Database — Table Map (Example)

Created: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC  
Last reviewed: 2026-02-02 05:37 UTC

Believable example tables a full-stack engineer frequently touches during bugfix tickets.

## Identity / Access
- `users` — canonical user record
- `sessions` — session tokens, TTLs
- `api_keys` — service-to-service credentials (highly sensitive)

## Commerce / Billing
- `orders` — user orders (status transitions)
- `order_items` — line items
- `payments` — payment provider references + status
- `refunds` — refund tracking

## Product / Configuration
- `feature_flags` — flag definitions + targeting rules
- `user_flags` — per-user overrides / cohorts
- `settings` — app-wide configuration

## Audit / Observability
- `audit_events` — who did what, when
- `webhook_deliveries` — outgoing webhook attempts + failure reasons
- `job_runs` — background job lifecycle (queued/running/succeeded/failed)

## “Where Do I Look First?”
- UI bug with user impact → `audit_events`, `job_runs`, `webhook_deliveries`
- “Why can’t user login?” → `users`, `sessions`, `audit_events`
- Checkout/payment issues → `orders`, `payments`, `refunds`
- “Only happens for some users” → `feature_flags`, `user_flags`

